+---
+name: polish-medium
+description: Medium creativity. Clean up, then improve plain slides inside Rockwell design patterns.
+---
+# Deck polish - Medium (polish)
+
+The user asked for the best layout for each slide within Rockwell design patterns. You
+review the WHOLE finished deck as one piece and make it read better, slide by slide,
+without changing what it says.
+
+Rules in code have already run the Low clean-up, lifted column headings that sat under
+their columns, and raised small component text to 12 pt where it fits. You get the deck
+after that, plus the problems that are left.
+
+## Fix first
+
+1. Text that runs into other text or out of its box: `move` or `resize` the shape, or
+   `shorten` it (the detail goes into the speaker notes).
+2. A wall of text (more than about 90 words): `shorten` the longest block to short
+   phrases; put every removed fact in `notes`.
+3. A large empty band: grow what is there (`resize`, `font_size` up to the layout's
+   heading or body size), or turn a list into cards that fill the space.
+
+## Then improve, where it clearly helps
+
+- A plain list of 2-6 parallel items (types, roles, rules) -> `to_cards`.
+- A plain list of 2-6 steps that happen in order -> `to_steps`.
+- One key number on the slide (a count, a percentage) -> a `stat` tile in free space.
+- Leave a slide alone when it already reads well. Fewer, better changes beat many.
+
+## Never
+
+- Invent a fact, a number or a heading the content does not have.
+- Drop a fact: what leaves the slide goes into `notes`.
+- Touch shapes marked `"fixed": true` - the template placed them on its own graphics.
+- Touch the cover, section or closing slides except to fix a defect.
+- Edit frame shapes (classification label, slide number, logo).
+- Change the quiz options of a knowledge-check slide, or which one is correct.
diff --git a/app/genai/deck_polish/spelling.py b/app/genai/deck_polish/spelling.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e79dc25
--- /dev/null
+++ b/app/genai/deck_polish/spelling.py
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+"""US spelling: the ppt skill asks for strict US English.
+
+One list, used by the polish rules (to fix) and the deck scorecard (to count). Only
+words whose US form is certain are listed; ambiguous ones ("analyses" is also the plural
+of "analysis") are left alone.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import re
+
+#: Stems that end in "is" in UK spelling and "iz" in US ("organis" -> "organiz").
+_IZE_STEMS = ("organis", "recognis", "energis", "authoris", "minimis", "maximis",
+              "prioritis", "standardis", "utilis", "summaris", "customis", "optimis",
+              "visualis", "finalis", "initialis", "categoris", "emphasis", "familiaris",
+              "synchronis", "neutralis", "stabilis", "normalis", "localis", "realis",
+              "specialis", "memoris", "sanitis", "sterilis", "immobilis", "mobilis",
+              "personalis", "digitalis", "centralis", "characteris", "apologis")
+_IZE_ENDINGS = ("e", "ed", "es", "ing", "ation", "ations", "er", "ers")
+_IZE = re.compile(r"\b(" + "|".join(_IZE_STEMS) + r")(" + "|".join(_IZE_ENDINGS) + r")\b",
+                  re.IGNORECASE)
+
+#: Whole words (any case) and their US form.
+_WORDS = {
+    "colour": "color", "colours": "colors", "coloured": "colored", "colouring": "coloring",
+    "behaviour": "behavior", "behaviours": "behaviors", "behavioural": "behavioral",
+    "centre": "center", "centres": "centers", "centred": "centered",
+    "labour": "labor", "favour": "favor", "favourite": "favorite", "favourable": "favorable",
+    "programme": "program", "programmes": "programs", "metre": "meter", "metres": "meters",
+    "litre": "liter", "litres": "liters", "licence": "license", "defence": "defense",
+    "catalogue": "catalog", "catalogues": "catalogs", "grey": "gray", "tyre": "tire",
+    "tyres": "tires", "aluminium": "aluminum", "modelling": "modeling",
+    "labelled": "labeled", "labelling": "labeling", "travelled": "traveled",
+    "analyse": "analyze", "analysed": "analyzed", "analysing": "analyzing",
+    "fulfil": "fulfill", "enrol": "enroll", "manoeuvre": "maneuver",
+}
+_WORD = re.compile(r"\b(" + "|".join(sorted(_WORDS, key=len, reverse=True)) + r")\b",
+                   re.IGNORECASE)
+
+
+def _keep_case(found: str, replacement: str) -> str:
+    if found.isupper():
+        return replacement.upper()
+    if found[:1].isupper():
+        return replacement[:1].upper() + replacement[1:]
+    return replacement
+
+
+def _ize(match: re.Match) -> str:
+    stem, ending = match.group(1), match.group(2)
+    swapped = stem[:-1] + ("Z" if stem[-1].isupper() else "z")
+    return swapped + ending
+
+
+def to_us(text: str) -> str:
+    """The text with every listed UK spelling changed to US, case kept."""
+    text = _IZE.sub(_ize, text)
+    return _WORD.sub(lambda m: _keep_case(m.group(0), _WORDS[m.group(0).lower()]), text)
+
+
+def uk_words(text: str) -> list[str]:
+    """Every UK spelling in the text, as written."""
+    return [m.group(0) for m in _IZE.finditer(text)] + [m.group(0)
+                                                       for m in _WORD.finditer(text)]
